## Flight report

**Left gate crossing:** Crossed during the k12→k13 transition (confirmed at decision k13): the forward camera showed no posts remaining and the downward camera showed the crossbar passing diagonally beneath. The approach leading up to it had the gap on the centre tick with comparable post sizes at k12, so the crossing was through the middle, not a graze — though the path there was messy (several back-ups and a wide loop through k9–k11 after an earlier crossing attempt at k6 swerved off-line and required backing off a close post twice).

**First mannequin sighting:** Decision k13/k14, right after the gate crossing — a standing grey/dark-clothed figure appeared roughly centred, very slightly nearer the R mark, beyond a low wooden table. I confirmed it was static (not the moving safety pilot) at k17 by backing away and returning: it reappeared at the same relative size and position, ruling out independent motion.

**Estimated room position:** Roughly x≈6–6.5, y≈0.3–0.5 (near a low table and a metal shelf/dresser against the far wall), based on where the drone closed to hover range.

**Final pose:** x≈5.63, y≈−0.02, z≈1.52, heading≈+9.5°, holding with zero velocity for the last several decisions.

**Assessment:** Yes — I believe the flight ended in front of the mannequin: it was centred and full head-to-feet in the forward panel at close range for the final four consecutive decisions (k20–k23) with negligible pose drift, consistent with a stable ~1 m hover facing it.

One caveat: at k16 I mistook proximity blur for movement and treated the figure briefly as the safety pilot, backing off before re-approaching and confirming it was static — no video review has been done here, so this is my visual read only, not a confirmed pass.
